<languages />
<translate>
<!--T:1-->
This page takes one change to production: planned in a pull request, merged, approved and applied. The example repository has two workspaces, one per directory, <code>network</code> and <code>dns</code>, and keeps their state in a remote backend.

<!--T:2-->
== Create the environments ==
Each workspace applies in a GitHub environment of the same name, and its required reviewers are who can approve the apply. The module creates them:
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="hcl" copy>
module "tacos" {
  source = "github.com/femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos?ref=v0.5.0"  # x-release-please-version

  repository     = "infra"
  environments   = ["network", "dns"]
  reviewer_teams = [github_team.deployer.id]
}
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:3-->
See [[Special:MyLanguage/Approvals|Approvals]] for who can approve and the permissions each job needs.

<!--T:4-->
== Add the workflow ==
Put this workflow in <code>.github/workflows/</code>, change the workspace list and add your credentials.
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="yaml" copy>
name: tofu
on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      workspace:
        description: The workspace to apply from this branch, once its environment approves.
        required: true
        type: choice
        options: &workspaces [network, dns]
permissions: {}
jobs:
  plan:
    name: ${{ matrix.workspace }} plan
    if: github.event_name != 'workflow_dispatch'
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        workspace: *workspaces
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
      pull-requests: write
    steps:
      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v0.5.0  # x-release-please-version
        with:
          step: plan
          workspace: ${{ matrix.workspace }}

      - uses: actions/checkout@9c091bb21b7c1c1d1991bb908d89e4e9dddfe3e0  # v7.0.0
        with:
          persist-credentials: false

      - uses: dflook/tofu-plan@c7416238983bdd94c5486fb856bb7358f2bcc935  # v3.1.0
        id: plan
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
        with:
          path: ${{ matrix.workspace }}

      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v0.5.0  # x-release-please-version
        with:
          step: changes
          workspace: ${{ matrix.workspace }}
          changes: ${{ steps.plan.outputs.changes }}
          plan-json: ${{ steps.plan.outputs.json_plan_path }}
          plan-text: ${{ steps.plan.outputs.text_plan_path }}

      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v0.5.0  # x-release-please-version
        if: always()
        with:
          step: collapse

  pending:
    needs: plan
    if: >-
      !cancelled() && (github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'
      || (github.event_name == 'push' && needs.plan.result == 'success'))
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      actions: write
      checks: read
    outputs:
      workspaces: ${{ steps.pending.outputs.workspaces }}
    steps:
      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v0.5.0  # x-release-please-version
        id: pending
        with:
          step: pending
          workspaces: ${{ inputs.workspace && format('["{0}"]', inputs.workspace) || '' }}

  apply:
    name: ${{ matrix.workspace }} apply
    needs: pending
    if: >-
      !cancelled() && needs.pending.result == 'success'
      && needs.pending.outputs.workspaces != '[]'
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        workspace: ${{ fromJSON(needs.pending.outputs.workspaces) }}
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    environment: ${{ matrix.workspace }}
    permissions:
      actions: read
      contents: read
      pull-requests: write
    steps:
      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v0.5.0  # x-release-please-version
        id: approver
        with:
          step: apply
          workspace: ${{ matrix.workspace }}

      - uses: actions/checkout@9c091bb21b7c1c1d1991bb908d89e4e9dddfe3e0  # v7.0.0
        with:
          persist-credentials: false

      - uses: dflook/tofu-apply@e3e5dfc8f935d4b152c767801046f63abf8a77d3  # v3.1.0
        id: apply
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
        with:
          path: ${{ matrix.workspace }}
          auto_approve: ${{ github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' }}

      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v0.5.0  # x-release-please-version
        if: always()
        with:
          step: result
          workspace: ${{ matrix.workspace }}
          outcome: ${{ steps.apply.outcome }}
          plan-json: ${{ steps.apply.outputs.json_plan_path }}
          plan-text: ${{ steps.apply.outputs.text_plan_path }}
          approver: ${{ steps.approver.outputs.approver }}

  # Make this the one required check
  gate:
    name: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && 'tofu gate' || 'tofu gate (pull requests only)' }}
    needs: plan
    if: always() && github.event_name == 'pull_request'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions: {}
    steps:
      - uses: femiwiki/terraform-github-tacos@v0.5.0  # x-release-please-version
        with:
          step: gate
          needs: ${{ toJSON(needs) }}
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:5-->
Then make the gate job's name, <code>tofu gate</code>, a required status check of the default branch, so a pull request whose plan fails cannot merge.

<!--T:6-->
== Open a pull request ==
Change a file in <code>network</code> and open a pull request. Each workspace is planned, and its plan is commented on the pull request. Nothing is applied yet.

<!--T:7-->
== Merge and approve ==
Merge the pull request. The run for the push plans every workspace again, and the <code>network apply</code> job waits for its environment. A reviewer opens the run and approves the deployment under "Review deployments".

<!--T:8-->
The apply makes a fresh plan and applies it only when it matches the one that was approved. The job summary shows who approved and what changed.

<!--T:9-->
== Next ==
* [[Special:MyLanguage/Runs|Runs]] says what each step of the workflow does.
* [[Special:MyLanguage/Auto apply|Auto apply]] skips the approval for chosen workspaces.
* [[Special:MyLanguage/Apply-before-merge|Apply-before-merge]] applies a pull request before it merges.
</translate>

